# Self-Review

Run an opinionated review of your changes **before** requesting human review. This is read-only -- it does not modify code or post comments to GitHub.

## Step 0 -- Determine review target

If `$ARGUMENTS` is a PR number or URL:
```bash
gh pr view "$ARGUMENTS" --json number,title,body,baseRefName,headRefName,additions,deletions,files
gh pr diff "$ARGUMENTS"
```

Otherwise, review the current branch against main:
```bash
git fetch origin main 2>/dev/null
git diff --name-status origin/main...HEAD
git diff --stat origin/main...HEAD
git log origin/main..HEAD --oneline
```

If no changes exist, stop and say "No changes to review."

## Step 1 -- Sanity gates

Run all gates. Report each as PASS or FAIL. Continue even if some fail.

### 1a. Conventional commit format
```bash
git log origin/main..HEAD --pretty='%s' | head -20
```
Every subject must match: `(feat|fix|docs|style|refactor|perf|test|build|ci|chore|revert)(\([\w-]+\))?: .+`

### 1b. Lint
```bash
pnpm nx affected -t lint --base=origin/main 2>&1 | tail -20
```

### 1c. Tests pass
```bash
pnpm nx affected -t test --base=origin/main 2>&1 | tail -30
```

### 1d. TypeScript compiles
```bash
pnpm nx affected -t typecheck --base=origin/main 2>&1 | tail -20
```

{{#ifHasStack config "go"}}
### 1e. Go lint + test
```bash
golangci-lint run ./... 2>&1 | tail -20
go test ./... -short -count=1 2>&1 | tail -20
```
{{/ifHasStack}}

{{#ifHasStack config "dotnet"}}
### 1e. .NET build + test
```bash
dotnet build --configuration Release 2>&1 | tail -10
dotnet test --configuration Release --no-build 2>&1 | tail -20
```
{{/ifHasStack}}

## Step 2 -- Deep review per file

Read each changed file. For each file, check the relevant items below based on file type.

### Architecture
- [ ] Module boundaries respected (no cross-app imports)
- [ ] Shared code in `libs/`, not duplicated across apps
- [ ] Workspace aliases used, not relative `../../` paths across packages
{{#if config.isPolyglot}}
- [ ] Go and Node.js apps do not share code directly
{{/if}}

### Code quality
- [ ] File size within limits (250 TS/TSX{{#ifHasStack config "go"}}, 400 Go{{/ifHasStack}}{{#ifHasStack config "dotnet"}}, 300 C#{{/ifHasStack}})
- [ ] Functions under 50 lines, max 5 parameters
- [ ] No god files (`utils.ts`, `helpers.go`, `common.cs`)
- [ ] Barrel exports for public APIs
- [ ] Naming conventions followed per stack rules
- [ ] No `any` in TypeScript
- [ ] No `console.log` in committed code
- [ ] No commented-out code blocks
- [ ] No TODO/FIXME without issue reference

### Security
- [ ] No secrets, tokens, or API keys in code
- [ ] Input validated at API boundaries
- [ ] No injection vulnerabilities (SQL, XSS, command)
- [ ] No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` without sanitization
{{#ifMultiTenancy config}}
- [ ] Tenant isolation maintained in all queries
- [ ] Tenant ID derived from session, not user input
{{/ifMultiTenancy}}

### Tests
- [ ] New public functions/endpoints/components have tests
- [ ] Tests cover happy path AND at least one error case
- [ ] No `test.skip` / `t.Skip()` without linked issue
- [ ] No snapshot tests for complex components
- [ ] Test files are next to source files

### Performance
- [ ] No N+1 queries
- [ ] No unnecessary re-renders in React components
- [ ] Database indexes present for queried/filtered columns
- [ ] List endpoints are paginated

{{#ifHasStack config "next-ssr"}}
### Next.js specific
- [ ] Server Components by default, `"use client"` only when needed
- [ ] `next/image` for images, `next/link` for navigation
- [ ] No functions passed from server to client components
{{/ifHasStack}}

{{#ifHasStack config "go"}}
### Go specific
- [ ] Hexagonal architecture respected (domain has zero external imports)
- [ ] `context.Context` as first parameter on public functions
- [ ] Errors wrapped: `fmt.Errorf("...: %w", err)`
- [ ] No `init()`, no global state, no bare `go` statements
{{/ifHasStack}}

{{#ifHasStack config "nestjs"}}
### NestJS specific
- [ ] Controllers are thin (delegate to services)
- [ ] Validation via class-validator DTOs + ValidationPipe
- [ ] No direct database access from controllers
{{/ifHasStack}}

{{#ifHasStack config "dotnet"}}
### .NET specific
- [ ] Feature folder pattern used
- [ ] FluentValidation for request validation
- [ ] Async all the way, no `.Result` or `.Wait()`
{{/ifHasStack}}

## Step 3 -- Output

```
## Self-Review Results

### BLOCKERS (must fix before merge)
- [file:line] Description

### WARNINGS (should fix, creates tech debt)
- [file:line] Description

### SUGGESTIONS (nice to have)
- [file:line] Description

### Sanity gates
- Commits: PASS/FAIL
- Lint: PASS/FAIL
- Tests: PASS/FAIL
- Typecheck: PASS/FAIL

### Verdict: READY / NOT READY
```

If zero blockers and zero gate failures: "Ready for human review."
Otherwise: "Not ready. Fix N blockers and M gate failures first."
